  "description": "While at its simplest, a frittata is nothing more than beaten eggs with some mix-ins cooked in a skillet, I like to go the extra mile to make them puffy. Somewhere between a soufflé and a Spanish-style tortilla. Ramps and eggs are also natural partners, and there are few egg recipes simpler for a crowd than a frittata.",
